/**
 * @defgroup spectral Spectral primitives
 * @brief Arrays, bases, coefficient transforms, 1D operators.
 *
 * Foundation layer: `Array`, `Dim_array`, `Base_spectral`, `Coef`, `Ope_1d`.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup fields Tensor fields and coordinate carriers
 * @brief `Scalar`, `Tensor`, `Vector`, `Metric`, coordinate-fields helpers.
 *
 * Built on top of @ref spectral. Owns spectral storage per domain via
 * `Val_domain`.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup domains Geometric domains
 * @brief `Domain`, `Space`, and concrete shells (spheric, polar, bispheric,
 * adapted, fourD-periodic, ...).
 *
 * Domains supply the topology, coordinate maps, and boundary information
 * over which @ref fields live.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup systems Equation systems and solvers
 * @brief `System_of_eqs`, equation registration (`add_eq_*`), Jacobian
 * column engine, MUMPS / Krylov linear solvers.
 *
 * Consumes @ref fields on @ref domains. Produces residual + Jacobian for
 * the Newton loop in `do_newton` / `do_newton_sparse`.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup utilities Utilities and IO
 * @brief Memory pools, parameter bags, binary IO sinks/sources, name tools.
 *
 * Cross-cutting helpers used by all other groups.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup eos Equations of state
 * @brief Cold and finite-temperature EOS tables, TOV solver.
 *
 * Self-contained subsystem under `include/hydro/`.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup metric Metric tensors
 * @brief 3+1 / conformal / AADS metric carriers.
 *
 * Built on @ref fields. Provide Christoffel symbols, Ricci, conformal
 * factor, lapse, shift, and contraction helpers consumed by @ref systems.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup util Low-level utilities
 * @brief `Array`, `Dim_array`, `Index`, `List_comp`, `Matrice`, `Param`.
 *
 * Containers, indexing primitives, parameter bags, dense matrix helper.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup Configurator Configurator subsystem
 * @brief TOML-backed runtime configuration for FUKa applications.
 *
 * Lives under `include/for_Kadath/config/`.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup fft FFTW interop
 * @brief Thin wrappers around FFTW for spectral basis transforms.
 */
